Chapter 1
Zhen Shi-yin encounters the Spiritual Jade in a dream;
Jia Yu-cun, in straitened circumstances, cherishes a woman of the inner rooms

Chapter 2
Jia Min dies in Yangzhou;
Leng Zi-xing describes the Rong mansion

Chapter 3
Jia Yu-cun is restored to office in Jinling;
Lin Dai-yu is taken into the Rong mansion

Grandmother Jia laughed. ‘Changing out of your clothes before you’ve even met our visitor! Go and greet your cousin.’
Bao-yu had already noticed the additional girl and guessed that she was his Aunt Lin’s daughter. He hurried over and bowed. When they had exchanged greetings and sat down again, he studied her features. She was unlike all the others:
Two mist-veiled brows, drawn together, yet not quite frowning;
Two dew-filled eyes, seeming glad, yet not quite glad.
Sorrow shaped the two dimples in her cheeks;
Illness lent its charm to all her slender body.
Her tears glimmered, drop by drop;
Her breath came in faint little gasps.
At rest, a lovely flower reflected in water;
In motion, a frail willow held by the wind.
Her heart had one opening more than Bi Gan’s;
Her frailty surpassed Xi Shi’s by three degrees.
After looking at her, Bao-yu said with a smile, ‘I have met this cousin before.’

Chapter 4
An ill-fated girl meets an ill-fated young man;
The Gourd Temple monk muddles a muddled case

Chapter 5
A visit to the Land of Illusion offers guidance through the Twelve Beauties;
Over immortal wine, songs unfold the Dream of the Red Chamber

[Kin Torn Apart]
A sail in wind and rain, a journey of three thousand li;
home and kin, all left behind.
Fearing tears will harm their declining years,
I tell my parents, ‘Do not worry about your child.
Hardship and advancement have always had their appointed course;
can meeting and parting be without their destined ties?
From now on we shall live in separate places;
let each keep safe and well.

Those in office, their family estates decline;
the wealthy and honoured, their gold and silver scattered.
Those who have shown kindness escape from death;
the heartless receive their plain reward.
Those owing life have paid with life;
those owing tears have exhausted them.
Wrong repaying wrong is no light matter;
partings and reunions were all ordained before.
To learn why life is short, ask of a former life;
even wealth and honour in old age are truly a lucky escape.
Those who see through it retreat into the Buddhist gate;
the deluded throw their lives away for nothing.
Like birds returning to the woods when all the food is gone,
they leave the great earth white and bare,
clean at last!

Chapter 6
Jia Bao-yu first tastes the love of cloud and rain;
Grannie Liu makes her first visit to the Rong mansion

Chapter 7
Palace flowers are delivered while Jia Lian dallies with Xi-feng;
At a feast in the Ning mansion Bao-yu meets Qin Zhong

Chapter 8
Comparing the Spiritual Jade, Oriole lets slip a hint;
Visiting Bao-chai, Dai-yu half betrays her jealousy

Chapter 9
Drawn by affection, two friends enter the family school;
Roused by suspicion, unruly boys turn the classroom upside down

Chapter 10
The widow Jin swallows an insult for the sake of gain;
Doctor Zhang examines an illness and traces its cause

Chapter 11
The Ning mansion lays on a family feast to celebrate a birthday;
At the sight of Xi-feng, Jia Rui is stirred to lust

Chapter 12
Wang Xi-feng lays a cruel trap for a lovesick man;
Jia Tian-xiang looks into the front of the Mirror of Love and Desire

Chapter 13
Qin Ke-qing is honoured in death as a Dragon Guard’s wife;
Wang Xi-feng helps to manage the Ning mansion

Chapter 14
Lin Ru-hai dies in the city of Yangzhou;
Jia Bao-yu pays his respects to the Prince of Beijing on the road

Chapter 15
Wang Xi-feng wields her influence at the Temple of the Iron Threshold;
Qin Jing-qing finds pleasure at Steamed-bun Hermitage

Chapter 16
Jia Yuan-chun’s talents win her a place in the Phoenix Splendour Palace;
Qin Jing-qing dies young and takes the road to the Yellow Springs

Chapter 17
In Prospect Garden, talent is tested in couplets and inscriptions;
At the Rong mansion, a homecoming celebrates the Lantern Festival

Chapter 18
Imperial grace allows Consort Yuan to visit her parents;
Amid the joys of family reunion, Bao-yu presents his verse

Chapter 19
On a tender night, a flower finds words for her heart;
In a quiet day’s lingering affection, jade gives forth fragrance

Chapter 20
Wang Xi-feng speaks firmly against jealousy;
Lin Dai-yu’s quick wit teases a sweet lisp

Chapter 21
Worthy Aroma chides Bao-yu with tender displeasure;
Pretty Patience saves Jia Lian with gentle words

Chapter 22
A song leads Bao-yu to an insight into Chan;
Lantern riddles sadden Jia Zheng with words of ill omen

‘Now that really is complete enlightenment,’ said Bao-chai. ‘Long ago Hui-neng, the Sixth Patriarch of the Southern School, came to Shaozhou when he first went in search of a teacher. Hearing that the Fifth Patriarch, Hong-ren, was at Huangmei, he went to serve as a kitchen monk. The Fifth Patriarch wanted to choose a successor to his teaching, so he ordered each of his disciples to compose a verse. The senior monk, Shen-xiu, said:
“The body is the bodhi tree;
The heart is like a stand for a bright mirror.
Diligently wipe it, time after time;
Let no dust remain.”

Chapter 23
Fine lines from The Western Chamber become words of teasing;
Passionate songs from The Peony Pavilion awaken a girl’s heart

Chapter 24
The Drunken Vajra esteems generosity and honour above wealth;
A lovestruck girl loses a handkerchief and awakens longing

Chapter 25
A sister and brother fall prey to the Five Ghosts through sorcery;
In the Dream of the Red Chamber, the Spiritual Jade meets two adepts

Chapter 26
Words contrived at Wasp-waist Bridge convey a secret longing;
Spring drowsiness at Naiad’s House gives voice to hidden feelings

Chapter 27
At Dripping Emerald Pavilion, Noble Consort Yang plays with bright-winged butterflies;
Beside the fragrant grave, Flying Swallow weeps for fallen petals

Chapter 28
Jiang Yu-han gives Qianxiang silk gauze in affection;
Xue Bao-chai wears red musk-scented beads in shy confusion

Now Lin Dai-yu had wrongly blamed Bao-yu for Skybright’s refusal to open the door the night before. The next day happened to be the day of farewell to the flowers. Her unspent anger was joined by sorrow at the passing of spring, and she had gathered some withered flowers and fallen petals to bury. Their fate reminded her irresistibly of her own. After weeping a little, she began to recite whatever lines came to her lips. She had no idea that Bao-yu was listening on the hillside. At first he merely nodded and sighed; but when he heard such lines as “Today I bury flowers, and people call me foolish;
In years to come, who knows who will bury me?” and “One day spring ends and beauty has grown old;
Flowers fall, people die, neither knowing of the other!”, he collapsed on the slope in an agony of grief, scattering the fallen flowers from the front of his robe. To think that Dai-yu, with her flower-like face and moon-like beauty, would one day be nowhere to be found: how could his heart not break? And if Dai-yu must one day vanish beyond all finding, so must Bao-chai, Caltrop, Aroma and the others. When Bao-chai and the rest could no longer be found, where would he himself be?

If he could not even tell where he would be, or where he would go, whose would this place be then, this garden, these flowers and willows? One thought led to another, and that to a third; he followed them round and round, until he scarcely knew what senseless thing he wished he might become, without a vestige of awareness, beyond creation’s reach and free of the world’s net, if only he could be released from this sorrow. As the lines say:
Flower-shadows never leave his side;
Birdsong sounds on either hand.

Chapter 29
One richly blessed prays still for further blessings;
A girl deep in love weighs love more deeply still

Chapter 30
Bao-chai seizes on a fan to aim two barbs;
Ling-guan traces ‘qiang’, and her absorption draws in an outsider

Chapter 31
Fans are torn for a smile worth a thousand gold pieces;
A qilin foreshadows two stars in white-haired old age

Chapter 32
Living Bao-yu, lost in feeling, lays bare his heart;
Golden, fierce in feeling, dies in shame

Chapter 33
A hostile brother watches his chance and speaks a few words;
An unworthy son is soundly beaten for his many faults

Chapter 34
Feeling within feeling moves a younger cousin’s heart;
Error upon error brings a brother mistaken counsel

Chapter 35
Silver Bai tastes the lotus-leaf soup herself;
Golden Oriole Huang deftly knots a plum-blossom cord

‘Today I bury flowers, and people call me foolish;
In years to come, who knows who will bury me?
See how, as spring ends, the flowers slowly fall:
That is the time when beauty grows old and dies.
One day spring ends and beauty has grown old;
Flowers fall, people die, neither knowing of the other!’

Chapter 36
Embroidered mandarin ducks attend a dream’s omen in Crimson Rue Studio;
Love’s allotted shares become clear at Pear-tree Court

Chapter 37
A Begonia Society takes shape by chance at Autumn Studio;
Chrysanthemum themes are devised by night at Allspice Court

Chapter 38
Lin the Naiad wins the chrysanthemum contest;
Xue of Allspice answers the crab poems with satire

Chapter 39
A village granny talks as fancy takes her;
A tender-hearted young cousin insists on getting to the bottom of it

Chapter 40
Old Lady Shi gives two feasts in Prospect Garden;
Faithful Jin calls three tiles in a drinking game

Chapter 41
At Green Bower Hermitage, tea is savoured with snow from plum blossom;
The House of Green Delights suffers an invasion by a mother locust

Chapter 42
With gentle words the Lady of Allspice dispels a habit of suspicion;
With polished wit the Naiad adds a lingering fragrance

Chapter 43
A birthday purse is made up for an idle day’s amusement;
For an affection not laid to rest, a pinch of earth serves as incense

Chapter 44
An unforeseen turn sends Xi-feng into a jealous rage;
Unexpected delight attends Patience’s toilette

Chapter 45
Kindred hearts open to each other in words of friendship;
On an evening of wind and rain, sorrow makes verses of wind and rain

Chapter 46
An awkward person cannot escape an awkward business;
Faithful vows never to be paired like mandarin ducks

Chapter 47
The blockhead tyrant’s advances earn him a savage beating;
The cold young gentleman flees to distant parts for fear of trouble

Chapter 48
An indiscriminate lover, thwarted in love, thinks of travelling to learn a trade;
A girl who longs for refinement labours over verse among the poets

Chapter 49
White snow and red plum blossom fill a world of glass;
Fragrant, powdered beauties cut raw meat and feast on venison

Chapter 50
At Reed Snow Lodge they vie in linking verses on the scene;
At Warm Fragrance Retreat they fashion elegant lantern riddles

Chapter 51
Young Miss Xue composes new poems on the past;
Quack Hu recklessly prescribes tiger-and-wolf drugs

Chapter 52
Charming Patience kindly conceals the theft of a shrimp-whisker bracelet;
Brave Skybright, though ill, mends a peacock-gold cloak

Chapter 53
At Ning mansion, New Year’s Eve brings worship in the ancestral shrine;
At Rong mansion, the Lantern Festival brings a night banquet

Chapter 54
Lady Dowager Shi exposes the stale old formulas;
Wang Xi-feng plays the dutiful child in motley

Chapter 55
A foolish concubine shames her daughter in a petty quarrel;
Crafty servants plot to deceive a young mistress

Chapter 56
Astute Tan-chun seeks new gains and sweeps away old abuses;
Discerning Bao-chai secures the general good with small kindnesses

Chapter 57
Clever Nightingale’s words test impetuous Bao-yu’s love;
Kindly Aunt Xue comforts lovelorn Dai-yu with tender words

Chapter 58
In apricot shade a false phoenix weeps for his make-believe mate;
Behind a madder-red gauze window true feeling weighs a lover’s foolish reasoning

Chapter 59
By Willow-leaf Islet, Oriole is scolded and Swallow berated;
In Crimson Rue Studio, generals are summoned and orders fly

Chapter 60
Jasmine powder takes the place of rose medicinal powder;
Rose essence brings a gift of fuling frost

Chapter 61
Bao-yu conceals a theft rather than break the vessel in striking the rat;
Patience uses her discretion to right a wrongful charge

Chapter 62
Guileless Xiang-yun sleeps drunk on a bed of peonies;
Innocent Caltrop unfastens a pomegranate-red skirt in a tender exchange

Chapter 63
The flowers hold a birthday feast by night at Green Delights;
A golden elixir brings death, and one fair woman conducts the mourning

Green phoenix plumes are bound into my broom;
At ease I tread Heaven’s gate and sweep the fallen flowers.
See the wind lift clouds of jade-bright dust.
One sudden plunge beneath that bank of cloud:
Beyond the gate, already the ends of earth!
Draw sword no more on Yellow Dragon, going wrong by just a thread;
Nor seek out poor old Dong’s wine-selling home again.
Let you and me lift our eyes towards the glowing clouds.
Dong-bin, when you have found your man, be quick to let me know;
Delay, and you will leave someone grieving among the peach flowers.

Chapter 64
A secluded maiden writes her grief in Songs of Five Beauties;
A libertine pledges love with a nine-dragon pendant

Chapter 65
Jia the Second secretly takes You Er-jie to wife;
You San-jie longs to marry Liu the Second
